# Day 32

## Experiment Title

Introduction to Maven and Build Automation


## Objective

To understand the basics of Apache Maven and study the process of build automation in Java applications.


## Theory

Apache Maven is a project management and build automation tool mainly used for Java applications. It helps developers manage project dependencies, compilation, testing, packaging, and deployment in a systematic manner.

Maven uses a configuration file called pom.xml which contains information about the project, required libraries, plugins, and build settings. Build automation reduces manual effort and improves the efficiency of software development.


## Requirements

Java Development Kit

Apache Maven

Windows Operating System


## Procedure

Install Apache Maven on the system.

Configure Maven environment variables properly.

Open the command prompt and verify the Maven installation.

Create a simple Maven project.

Observe the Maven project structure and configuration files.


## Output

Apache Maven was installed and configured successfully.

The Maven environment was verified successfully through the command prompt.

A basic Maven project structure was created successfully.


## Result

Successfully understood the basics of Apache Maven and build automation.
